From: Chris Bongaarts <cab@bongalow.net>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 18:40:37 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] 10225: Decompiler: discard a jump-table override for
 unreached flow instead of crashing

Decompiler: discard a jump-table override that flow never
 reaches instead of crashing in switchOver

A jump-table override is linked to its BRANCHIND only if flow reaches that
address. When it is never reached (a preceding call marked non-returning, a
call-return flow override), the JumpTable keeps a null indirect op, and
switchOverJumpTables passes it to JumpTable::switchOver, which dereferences it
and kills the decompiler process.

Drop such tables at the end of flow, as truncatedFlow already does for a
partial clone, so installSwitchDefaults, structureReset's dead-table filter and
ActionSwitchNorm only see tables that are linked to a BRANCHIND.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NvtBaRRAc3SfKXLzLpASbV
---
 .../src/decompile/cpp/funcdata_block.cc           | 15 +++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Ghidra/Features/Decompiler/src/decompile/cpp/funcdata_block.cc b/Ghidra/Features/Decompiler/src/decompile/cpp/funcdata_block.cc
index 45aee2afd3..08578362a9 100644
--- a/Ghidra/Features/Decompiler/src/decompile/cpp/funcdata_block.cc
+++ b/Ghidra/Features/Decompiler/src/decompile/cpp/funcdata_block.cc
@@ -693,14 +693,25 @@ JumpTable *Funcdata::recoverJumpTable(Funcdata &partial,PcodeOp *op,FlowInfo *fl
 
 /// For each jump-table, for each address, the corresponding basic block index is computed.
 /// This also calculates the \e default branch for each jump-table.
+/// A jump-table override whose BRANCHIND was never reached by the flow has no PcodeOp to
+/// work from, and is discarded.
 /// \param flow is the flow object (mapping addresses to p-code ops)
 void Funcdata::switchOverJumpTables(const FlowInfo &flow)
 
 {
+  vector<JumpTable *> remain;
   vector<JumpTable *>::iterator iter;
 
-  for(iter=jumpvec.begin();iter!=jumpvec.end();++iter)
-    (*iter)->switchOver(flow);
+  for(iter=jumpvec.begin();iter!=jumpvec.end();++iter) {
+    JumpTable *jt = *iter;
+    if (jt->getIndirectOp() == (PcodeOp *)0) {	// Override that the flow never linked to a BRANCHIND
+      delete jt;
+      continue;
+    }
+    jt->switchOver(flow);
+    remain.push_back(jt);
+  }
+  jumpvec = remain;
 }
 
 void Funcdata::installSwitchDefaults(void)
